    "interpretation": "The R22 (SH0ES) Cepheid reduction shows an X_i-dependent offset relative to MF2023, indicating that the R22 P-L fitting absorbs part of the TEP signal. The MF2023 VI Cepheid distances (same team as the JWST TRGB distances) recover the correct TEP negative slope, while the R22 distances give a positive (wrong-sign) slope. This is consistent with the TEP prediction that different Cepheid reductions absorb the potential-dependent clock bias to different degrees."
